# DOCUMENT 2: MEDICAL AESTHETICS INDUSTRY INTELLIGENCE

## INJECTABLES & NEUROTOXINS

Botox (onabotulinumtoxinA) — Allergan/AbbVie. Market leader.
The standard against which everything is measured.

Dysport (abobotulinumtoxinA) — Galderma. Faster onset,
broader diffusion. Preferred by practitioners who want
natural movement over frozen results.

Xeomin (incobotulinumtoxinA) — Merz. Naked toxin —
no complexing proteins. Preferred for patients with
potential resistance.

Daxxify (daxibotulinumtoxinA) — Revance. Extended duration
(up to 6 months). The disruptor.

Jeuveau — Evolus. Positioned as the "newtox" —
millennial-facing, price competitive.

## DERMAL FILLERS

Juvederm family (Allergan) — HA based. Voluma, Vollure,
Volbella, Volux. The dominant portfolio.

Restylane family (Galderma) — HA based. Lyft, Silk,
Contour, Kysse. Known for precision.

Sculptra (Galderma) — PLLA. Collagen stimulator.
Longer lasting. Requires patience and technique mastery.

Radiesse (Merz) — CaHA. Immediate + collagen stimulation.

RHA Collection (Revance) — Dynamic HA. Designed to move
with facial expressions.

Belotero (Merz) — Fine line specialist.

## ENERGY BASED DEVICES

Ultherapy — HIFU. Skin tightening. Falling out of favor
due to pain and inconsistent results.

Thermage — RF. Still respected for skin tightening.

Morpheus8 — RF microneedling. InMode. Currently dominant.

Sofwave — Newer HIFU. Better patient experience than Ulthera.

CoolSculpting — Cryolipolysis. Allergan. Mass market
body contouring.

Emsculpt NEO — BTL. Muscle + fat simultaneously.

Emface — BTL. Facial muscle + skin. The new category.

## SKINCARE & ADJUNCTS

Skinbetter Science — owned by Allergan. Professional
recommended, DTC restricted.

ZO Skin Health — Zein Obagi. Aggressive protocols.
Physician-grade.

SkinMedica — Allergan. TNS technology. Science forward.

Alastin — wound healing and procedure optimization.

Epicutis — luxury medical skincare. Small, intentional.
The brand that belongs in this room.

## KEY CLINICAL CONCEPTS

The liquid facelift — filler repositioning vs volumizing.

The 8-point lift — Mauricio de Maio protocol.

Facial thirds — upper, mid, lower. How masters think
about proportion.

The danger zones — angular artery, supratrochlear,
infraorbital. What separates careful from careless.

Cannula vs needle — the philosophy split that reveals
clinical personality.

The less is more movement — micro-dosing,
natural results, the Allergan Beautiful Skin study.

Combination therapy — device + injectable + skincare
as a single treatment philosophy.

Patient psychology — the mirror problem,
body dysmorphia recognition, the ethical injector.

## BUSINESS OF AESTHETICS

Average revenue per patient: $800–$2,400/visit
in premium practices.

Membership models — monthly loyalty programs disrupting
the traditional visit model.

The Alle/Aspire/Xperience loyalty programs —
how reps use them to lock practitioners in.

GPO vs direct buy — the purchasing decision that
defines practice economics.

The med spa vs physician office split —
different clientele, different economics, different ego.

KOL (Key Opinion Leader) structure —
how Allergan, Galderma, Merz, Evolus build influence.

Congress calendar — ASDS, AMWC, IMCAS, Vegas Cosmetic
Surgery, Aesthetics Next — where the real conversations happen.

## PRACTITIONER ARCHETYPES

The Artist — technique-obsessed, result-driven,
often independent. Values peer recognition over revenue.

The Entrepreneur — practice builder, team focused,
thinks in systems and scale.

The Academic — injector who teaches, writes, presents.
Peer-reviewed. Cautious about claims.

The Loyalist — brand loyal, relationship driven,
the rep's best friend and biggest defender.

The Skeptic — evidence-based, slow to adopt,
but influential when they do.

The Influencer — built a following, content-forward,
understands the attention economy.

