# DOCUMENT 14: GEO INTELLIGENCE — ATLANTA, GA

THE ROOM IN ONE SENTENCE:
Atlanta is the most powerful
aesthetic market in the South —
a city that built itself on ambition, reinvention,
and the unshakeable belief that presentation matters.

MELANIN-RICH SKIN — THE DEFINING CLINICAL ISSUE:
The standard aesthetic training in the United States
was developed primarily for Fitzpatrick I-III skin types.
The Atlanta patient is predominantly Fitzpatrick IV-VI.
This changes everything:
- Filler placement and depth
- Neurotoxin dosing and pattern
- Device selection and settings
- Complication risk profile

THE ALD DIVERSITY IMPERATIVE:
The Atlanta practitioner at the ALD table
is not there for diversity —
they are there because the room
is incomplete without the clinical perspective
that comes from serving the most
diverse patient population
in American aesthetic medicine.

THE CONCIERGE QUESTION FOR ATLANTA:
"You practice in the market with the most clinically complex
and underserved patient population
in American aesthetic medicine.
What do you know about treating melanin-rich skin
that the rest of the industry needs to hear
and hasn't figured out yet?"

